<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Zalmaqum</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 BCE – 1700 BCE (approx.) · capital Harran</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Zalmaqum, a league of small kingdoms around Harran in the Balikh valley, known from the Mari letters of the 18th century BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Zalmaqum was the name of a region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balikh-river">Balikh</a> river. In the 18th century BCE its four kings acted together as a loose confederacy, alongside the Amorite tribal groups who moved seasonally through the steppe.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mari">Mari</a> archives record that the kings of Zalmaqum and Yaminite tribal leaders swore an alliance in the temple of the moon god Sin at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a>, already an important sanctuary. They negotiated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yamhad">Yamhad</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-upper-mesopotamia">Kingdom of Upper Mesopotamia</a>, but no texts from the confederacy itself survive.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The confederacy disappears from the record after the fall of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mari">Mari</a> c. 1760 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> remained a major city and centre of the moon cult into the Islamic period.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1800 BCE – 1700 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:23.88%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 BCE – 1700 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Harran</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Asdi-takim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Mesopotamian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Amorite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zalmaqum confederacy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1750&amp;focus=zalmaqum" aria-label="Zalmaqum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5659 849 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Zalmaqum lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5979 1105L6039 1183"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6039 1183h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5979 1105h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5979 1105h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Harran. <a href="/atlas?year=-1750&amp;focus=zalmaqum">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

